The variation with time $t$ of the potential difference (p.d.) $V$ across the load resistor is shown in Fig. 8.2.

{{figure:figure_8_2}}

A capacitor is now connected between points C and D of the bridge rectifier. This results in smoothing of the p.d. across the load resistor. The difference between the maximum and minimum values of the smoothed p.d. is 33% of the peak p.d. $V_0$.
